---
import Studio from '../layouts/Studio.astro';
import { apps, playUrl } from '../data/apps';
---
<Studio title="Website privacy · Sazen" description="Privacy information for the Sazen app collection website.">
  <article class="legal band">
    <header class="legal-head">
      <a class="back reveal" href="/">← Back to Sazen</a>
      <span class="eyebrow reveal">Website privacy · 23 October 2026</span>
      <h1 class="display lines"><span><span>A simple website.</span></span><span><span class="ghost">A simple policy.</span></span></h1>
      <p class="reveal">This page applies to the Sazen website. Each mobile app has its own privacy policy.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="legal-body">
      <section class="reveal">
        <h2>What this website collects</h2>
        <p>This is a static website. It does not have accounts, contact forms, advertising, or analytics scripts. It does not set cookies or store your preferences. Fonts and app images are served from this website.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="reveal">
        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>Cloudflare Pages hosts this website. Cloudflare processes connection information, such as IP addresses and request details, to serve and protect the site. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a> for details.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="reveal">
        <h2>App websites and Google Play</h2>
        <p>Links to app websites and Google Play take you to services with their own policies. For information about an app’s data, permissions, support, or deletion options, follow its “App support” and “Data safety” sections on Google Play:</p>
        <ul class="legal-apps">{apps.map(app => <li><a href={playUrl(app)} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{app.name}{app.slug === '99-names' ? ' – Asmaul Husna' : ''} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>)}</ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Studio>
